LID - e71204
AB  - A wandering spleen (WS) is rare and often presents a diagnostic challenge to 
      clinicians. We report a WS in a 16-year-old who presented with abdominal pain, 
      vomiting, and peritonism. Imaging (ultrasound and CT scans), which usually 
      facilitates a prompt diagnosis, was inconclusive, and the diagnosis was made by 
      exploratory laparotomy.
