TI  - The Wanderer: Acute Abdomen Secondary to a Wandering Spleen.
PG  - 6697671
LID - 10.1155/crra/6697671 [doi]
LID - 6697671
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare condition resulting from the absence or laxity of 
      peritoneal attachments, allowing the spleen to migrate within the abdominal 
      cavity. While some patients may remain asymptomatic, others can develop 
      life-threatening complications such as splenic torsion, infarction, and bowel 
      obstruction. This case report highlights one of the complications of wandering 
      spleen and the importance of timely diagnosis and intervention.
