TI  - Case report: laparoscopic keyhole splenopexy with composite mesh for wandering 
      spleen.
PG  - 1261-1264
LID - 10.1007/s13304-025-02181-6 [doi]
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare condition that can necessitate urgent laparotomic 
      splenectomy. Prompt recognition of symptoms is crucial for preserving the spleen 
      by performing laparoscopic splenopexy. We present a laparoscopic technique that 
      enables safe and durable splenopexy using a composite keyhole-shaped mesh 
      (13-month follow-up).
