TI  - Computed tomography features and surgical treatment of wandering spleen torsion: 
      A case report.
PG  - 6213-6216
LID - 10.1016/j.radcr.2024.08.146 [doi]
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare clinical entity characterized by the laxity, absence, 
      or abnormal attachment of splenic supporting ligaments leading to hypermobility 
      and abnormal positioning of the spleen in the abdominal cavity. The abnormally 
      increased mobility of the spleen predisposes it to torsion and infarction. 
      Authors present a case of wandering spleen complicated to torsion and infarct in 
      a middle aged lady. The patient presented with acute abdominal pain, diagnosed by 
      abdominal computed tomography and underwent surgery and splenectomy.
