TI  - Case Report: Gut and spleen anomalies associated with DYRK1A syndrome.
PG  - 936732
LID - 10.3389/fped.2022.936732 [doi]
LID - 936732
AB  - DYRK1A syndrome has been extensively studied primarily with regard to neurologic 
      and other phenotypic features such as skeleton and craniofacial alterations. In 
      the present paper, we aim to highlight unusual anomalies associated with a DYRK1A 
      mutation: a 17-year-old female patient with language and cognitive delay, 
      microcephaly, and an autistic disorder, who was operated upon for spleen torsion 
      with anomalous gut fixation.
