TI  - Torsed wandering spleen as a cause of recurrent abdominal pain in a child.
PG  - 1794-1797
LID - 10.1016/j.radcr.2022.03.017 [doi]
AB  - Wandering spleen is an uncommon cause of acute abdomen in children. Diagnosis of 
      this condition is challenging due to its non-specific symptoms, varying intensity 
      and protracted history of presentation. Radiographs and ultrasound imaging 
      provide rapid and reliable means to diagnose this condition without exposure to 
      excessive radiation. We present a case of a torsed wandering spleen in a child 
      with recurrent abdominal pain. We highlight the role of imaging in identifying 
      salient radiographic and sonographic signs for diagnosis.
