TI  - Torsion of a Wandering Spleen Managed Conservatively: Rare and Interesting.
PG  - 323-325
LID - 10.4103/jiaps.JIAPS_216_19 [doi]
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare pathology. A 2-year-old child with abdominal pain was 
      diagnosed to have a torted, avascular wandering spleen. On conservative 
      management, she remains well with no radiological evidence of the spleen. Splenic 
      torsion usually warrants surgery. Nonoperative management in selected cases 
      allows the natural process of autosplenectomy.
