TI  - Wandering spleen: A rare entity and a diagnostic dilemma.
PG  - 389-391
LID - 10.4103/ijri.IJRI_46_20 [doi]
AB  - Wandering spleen refers to a spleen that is ectopic in its location contrary to a 
      normal spleen which rests in the left hypochondrium. Although it is a rare 
      clinical entity seen in children, it can also be rarely seen in females of 
      reproductive age group. We present one such case of wandering spleen which was 
      misdiagnosed earlier as a sub-hepatic collection.
