TI  - Pelvic splenosis-A rare cause of pelvic mass.
PG  - 2247-2249
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.2419 [doi]
AB  - Splenosis is a medical condition that seldom occurs after splenic tissue spillage 
      via trauma or surgery. Ectopic spleen tissues can be found almost anywhere within 
      the body. Albeit benign, it is often misdiagnosed as a tumor. Surgery is not 
      indicated unless symptomatic. The imaging of choice for pelvic splenosis, 
      although conventional, is a sulfur colloid nuclear scintigraphy.
