TI  - Diagnostic imaging of abnormalities in the number and location of the spleen.
PG  - 26-34
LID - S0033-8338(18)30129-2 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.rx.2018.07.002 [doi]
AB  - In imaging studies, some developmental anomalies such as perisplenic accessory 
      spleen are easily recognizable due to their high incidence. However, other, less 
      common anomalies such as intrapancreatic accessory spleen, splenopancreatic 
      fusion, splenogonadal fusion, heterotaxy, and wandering spleen, as well as 
      acquired conditions such as splenosis, can pose diagnostic difficulties. This aim 
      of this review is to show the imaging diagnosis and differential diagnoses of 
      these uncommon splenic anomalies.
