IS  - 0015-5659 (Linking)
VI  - 77
IP  - 2
DP  - 2018
TI  - Wandering spleen: a unique cause of acute abdomen.
PG  - 400-402
LID - 10.5603/FM.a2017.0097 [doi]
AB  - We present the case of a 16-year-old boy presented with 2-week episode of 
      wor-sening lower abdominal pain. Clinically, there was a tender palpable mass on 
      the suprapubic region. Ultrasonography showed an absent spleen at its usual area, 
      instead suprapubic mass suggestive of ectopic spleen was identified. An 
      emer-gency laparotomy revealed a congested spleen in the pelvic cavity. 
      Splenectomy was undertaken as it was non-viable. The patient was discharged 
      uneventfully with triple vaccinations. We describe this unique entity with its 
      literature review. (Folia Morphol 2018; 77, 2: 400-402).
