VI  - 179
IP  - 25
DP  - 2017 Jun 19
TI  - [Wandering spleen in a patient hospitalized with acute abdomen].
LID - V01170025 [pii]
AB  - An 11-year-old girl was hospitalized with a two-day history of lower abdominal 
      pain. The patient had a localized peritoneal reaction in the right lower 
      quadrant, an elevated C-reactive protein level, and an increased white blood cell 
      count. On the suspicion of acute appendicitis a diagnostic laparoscopy was 
      performed. This revealed a misplaced spleen in the right side of the pelvis with 
      a partly torsion of a long vascular pedicle. The splenic tissue was vital without 
      any sign of ischaemia. However, splenopexy was not possible, and an uncomplicated 
      elective splenectomy was performed.
