TI  - Multiple Cardiac Papillary Fibroelastomas.
PG  - 104-106
LID - 10.1016/j.case.2017.03.004 [doi]
AB  - * We present a case of a patient who presented with symptoms of heart failure and 
      was found to have multiple cardiac masses. The mass attached to the right atrial 
      lead and the mass in the left ventricle were the largest. * The patient underwent 
      cardiac surgery and 9 to ten masses were resected with biopsy consistent with 
      papillary fibroelastomas. * There was tissue in the right atrium that resembled 
      ectopic spleen.
