DP  - 2017 Mar
TI  - Portal venous thrombosis developing after torsion of a wandering spleen.
PG  - 394-396
LID - 10.4103/1119-3077.201431 [doi]
AB  - Torsion of a wandering spleen is a rare disease. The symptoms and signs of this 
      condition are only present when the splenic pedicle torts. The etiological 
      factors are the congenital absence of the ligaments that hold the spleen in its 
      normal anatomic position, or the relaxation of these ligaments resulting from 
      conditions like trauma and abdominal surgery. We aimed to present a rare case 
      with torsion of wandering spleen that consequently developed thrombosis of portal 
      vein and its branches, taking into consideration the relevant literature.
