TI  - Torsion of a wandering spleen. A rare cause of acute abdomen.
PG  - 1490-2
LID - 10.15537/smj.2015.12.12363 [doi]
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare condition that accounts for less than 0.25% of all 
      indications for splenectomy. It is characterized by ectopic localization of the 
      spleen owing to the lack or weakening of its ligaments. Torsion is the most 
      common complication due to its long pedicle and high mobility, which may result 
      in acute abdomen. We report a case of torsion in a wandering spleen in a 
      28-year-old male presenting with an acute abdomen that was treated by 
      splenectomy.
