TI  - Dynamic MRI in the diagnosis and post surgical evaluation of wandering spleen.
PG  - 15-22
LID - 10.3941/jrcr.v8i10.1969 [doi]
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare but potentially clinically significant entity, and may 
      be a cause for a patient presenting with acute abdomen. Because wandering spleen 
      may present with non-specific symptoms and presentation, it can be a difficult 
      diagnosis to make clinically. This paper describes a case report of the use of 
      dynamic Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) in a young woman to confirm the 
      diagnosis of wandering spleen pre-operatively. The patient underwent a splenopexy 
      and a post-operative MRI confirmed the successful surgical fixation of the 
      patient's spleen.
