TI  - Multidetector computed tomography diagnosis of splenic flexure volvulus: 
      usefulness of multiplanar reformats.
PG  - e79-82
AB  - Splenic flexure volvulus is the least common form of colonic volvulus. 
      Preoperative radiological diagnosis is usually made presumptively, based on plain 
      radiographs and/or barium contrast enema study in patients presenting with acute 
      large bowel obstruction. We report a case in which multidetector computer 
      tomography (CT) findings were diagnostic of this condition, thus highlighting the 
      usefulness of multiplanar reformatting.
