VI  - 71
IP  - 1
DP  - 2012 Feb
TI  - Intrapancreatic accessory spleen.
PG  - 45-7
AB  - A case of accessory spleen located in the tail of the pancreas in a stillbirth 
      male foetus is reported. The congenital anomaly was revealed at autopsy. The 
      intrapancreatic spleen was well demarcated and was composed of red and white 
      pulp; however, same pancreatic ducts were intermingled with the splenic 
      parenchyma. As well as the intrapancreatic lesion another minute accessory spleen 
      was also found at the hilum of the proper organ. Since a lack of morphological 
      features of trisomy 13 syndrome were found in the foetus, the ectopic spleens 
      were regarded as incidental findings.
