TI  - The wandering spleen: an unusual case of thrombocytopenia.
PG  - 161-3
LID - 10.2147/JBM.S24168 [doi]
AB  - Thrombocytopenia is a common laboratory finding in current medical practices. The 
      workup of thrombocytopenia can be challenging with numerous causes that can be 
      included in the differential diagnosis. Thrombocytopenia can be due to bone 
      marrow hypoproliferation, peripheral destruction, or sequestration. This paper 
      presents a case of isolated thrombocytopenia in a young female and discusses the 
      causes of thrombocytopenia.
