VI  - 52
IP  - 8
DP  - 2011 Oct 1
TI  - Wandering spleen with torsion and complete infarction.
PG  - 911-3
LID - 10.1258/ar.2011.100504 [doi]
AB  - Wandering spleen is rare and is associated with a high incidence of splenic 
      torsion and infarction. Presenting symptoms range from an asymptomatic, 
      incidentally palpated abdominal mass to an acutely ill patient. Because wandering 
      spleen is uncommon in the pediatric population, a heightened awareness of the 
      condition is required for accurate diagnosis and appropriate management. We 
      present a case of a 4-year-old girl who presented with acute abdomen and was 
      surgically confirmed to have a wandering spleen with torsion and complete 
      infarction.
