TI  - Laparoscopic splenopexy for wandering spleen: case report and review of the 
      literature.
PG  - e182-4
LID - 10.1097/SLE.0b013e3181f69ce2 [doi]
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare condition in which the spleen lacks retroperitoneal 
      fixation, thus its vascular pedicle can twist resulting in ischemia. Although 
      splenectomy has traditionally been used for this condition, splenopexy is 
      increasingly used in the pediatric population to anchor the spleen and preserve 
      splenic function. We report an unusual case of wandering spleen in an adult with 
      chronic torsion managed with laparoscopic splenopexy, suggesting splenic 
      preservation is possible in adults with this presentation as well.
