PMID- 19735802
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20091209
LR  - 20220419
IS  - 1531-5037 (Electronic)
IS  - 0022-3468 (Linking)
VI  - 44
IP  - 9
DP  - 2009 Sep
TI  - Accessory spleen torsion: rare cause of acute abdomen in children and review of 
      literature.
PG  - e15-8
LID - 10.1016/j.jpedsurg.2009.06.029 [doi]
AB  - Torsion of an accessory spleen is an extremely rare condition. We describe an 
      unusual case of acute abdomen caused by torsion of an accessory spleen in a 
      12-year-old boy. The patient underwent a laparotomy with splenectomy; the course 
      was favorable. We discuss the clinical findings and values of preoperative 
      instrumental diagnosis. The literature is also reviewed. This is the 11th case 
      reported in the English literature. Torsion of an accessory spleen should be 
      considered in the differential diagnosis of acute abdomen or subacute abdominal 
      pain.
