VI  - 43
IP  - 5
DP  - 2008 May
TI  - Familial wandering spleen: a first instance.
PG  - E23-5
LID - 10.1016/j.jpedsurg.2007.12.077 [doi]
AB  - We report on 2 sisters presenting with acute torsion of a wandering spleen within 
      a 3-year interval. The diagnosis was made preoperatively by computed tomography 
      (CT) in both cases. A high index of suspicion because of our experience with the 
      first patient, who underwent splenectomy, enabled a correct early diagnosis in 
      the sibling. On urgent surgery, reversible ischemic changes were found, and 
      detorsion and splenopexy resulted in preservation of the spleen.
