VI  - 167
IP  - 33
DP  - 2005 Aug 15
TI  - [Wandering spleen].
PG  - 3058-9
AB  - The spleen is well fixed below the left side of the diaphragm. Wandering spleen 
      is a rare condition of unknown pathogenesis. The wandering spleen is most often 
      localized in the lower abdomen or pelvis. The diagnosis may be difficult if 
      wandering spleen is not suspected. Often a wandering spleen can be palpated in 
      the lower abdomen. In the rare cases of torsion of the splenic vascular pedicle, 
      wandering spleen becomes symptomatic, and splenectomy should be performed. We 
      report a case of a 20-year-old female treated with splenectomy because of torsion 
      of the vascular pedicle.
