TI  - [Case report: Acute abdomen and pelvic mass due to torsion of a wandering 
      spleen].
PG  - 105-7
AB  - Torsioned wandering spleen should be considered in patients who have an 
      intrapelvic mass with acute abdominal symptoms. Nowadays, color Doppler US and CT 
      are easily achievable and are highly accurate for indicating the correct 
      diagnosing in such patients. Using these two modalities together will increase 
      the ability for correct diagnosis.
