TI  - The split notochord syndrome with dorsal enteric fistula.
PG  - 729-30
AB  - The authors describe a new case of the split notochord syndrome (SNS) with dorsal 
      enteric fistula in an eight-month-old-boy. The child had also central nervous 
      system anomalies including dysgenetic corpus callosum, absence of septum 
      pellucidum, triventricular hydrocephalus, small posterior fossa, and 
      lipomyelomeningocele, gastrointestinal system anomalies such as malrotation, 
      wandering spleen, and right inguinal hernia. The clinical features, 
      embryogenesis, and literature were reviewed briefly.
