VI  - 85
IP  - 4
DP  - 2000 Oct-Dec
TI  - Internal herniation of wandering spleen--a rare cause of recurrent abdominal 
      pain.
PG  - 322-4
AB  - A rare case of wandering spleen herniating through a defect in transverse 
      mesocolon, which was managed electively by splenopexy using polyglycolic acid 
      mesh is reported. An enlarged wandering spleen is at constant risk of trauma, 
      torsion and infarction. Internal herniation seems to increase the above risks. 
      Early recognition and elective splenopexy should be the treatment of choice.
