TI  - Accessory spleen torsion: US, CT and MR findings.
PG  - 509-12
AB  - Torsion of an accessory spleen is a very unusual entity that can appear with 
      abdominal pain associated with the presence of an avascular mass. We report the 
      case of a 13-year-old boy with torsion and infarction of an accessory spleen 
      presenting as a painful abdominal mass in which imaging examination with US, CT 
      and MR showed a large avascular mass in the upper left abdomen.
