TI  - [Unusual testicular tumor: an ectopic spleen].
PG  - 67-9
AB  - The authors report a case of discontinuous splenogonadal fusion diagnosed after 
      left orchidectomy. Ectopic spleen in the scrotum is a rare congential anomaly 
      frequently associated with other anomalies, especially limb defects. The 
      diagnosis is difficult. Preoperative isotope scanning and intraoperative 
      pathological examination can be performed to avoid unnecessary orchidectomy.
