TI  - A case of wandering spleen causing urinary symptoms after correction of a 
      posterolateral diaphragmatic hernia.
PG  - 602-3
AB  - A 12-year-old girl who had had an operation for a posterolateral diaphragmatic 
      hernia was admitted to the hospital because of enuresis. Physical examination and 
      radiologic studies revealed the spleen behind the urinary bladder, left-sided 
      hydronephrosis, and a high volume of residual urine. The hydronephrosis and 
      residual urine resolved immediately following splenectomy.
