TI  - Intrauterine torsion of a wandering spleen presenting as an abdominal cystic 
      swelling.
PG  - 1508-10
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare clinical condition that presents commonly with splenic 
      infarction secondary to torsion. Intrauterine torsion of a wandering spleen, 
      however, is extremely rare. An unusual case of intrauterine torsion of a 
      wandering spleen presenting as an abdominal mass is reported.
