PMID- 10800003
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20000620
LR  - 20190905
IS  - 0091-2751 (Print)
IS  - 0091-2751 (Linking)
VI  - 28
IP  - 5
DP  - 2000 Jun
TI  - Power Doppler sonographic diagnosis of torsion in a wandering spleen.
PG  - 246-8
AB  - A wandering spleen is a rare clinical entity resulting from congenital 
      maldevelopment or acquired laxity of the spleen's suspensory ligaments; it may 
      result in torsion of the spleen. We report the gray-scale sonographic, power 
      Doppler sonographic, and CT findings in a case of wandering spleen torsion. The 
      gray-scale sonograms showed a displaced spleen that appeared as a homogeneous, 
      hypoechoic mass suggestive of an enlarged, ectopic spleen in the central abdomen. 
      Power Doppler sonograms showed no blood flow in the parenchyma or hilum of the 
      spleen and were consistent with torsion and infarction in the spleen. 
      Contrast-enhanced CT scans showed a homogeneous, unenhanced mass that was 
      diagnosed as a torsioned wandering spleen. The hilar vessels of the spleen were 
      also unenhanced.
