IS  - 0028-2162 (Linking)
VI  - 142
IP  - 34
DP  - 1998 Aug 22
TI  - [A wandering spleen].
PG  - 1927-9
AB  - A mobile asymptomatic abdominal mass was accidentally found in a 81-year-old man. 
      Further studies revealed a wandering spleen. Wandering spleen is rare, the 
      diagnosis can easily be made with ultrasonography. The patient presented was 
      asymptomatic, but severe complications may occur. Congenital anomalies of 
      ligaments, splenomegaly and pregnancy may be of aetiological importance. In young 
      patients and in case of complaints splenopexia is the treatment of choice; the 
      patient presented was treated conservatively.
