TI  - Gastric volvulus in childhood.
PG  - 46-7
AB  - Gastric volvulus is an uncommon condition more so in the paediatric age group. 
      The cause of gastric volvulus may be idiopathic or secondary to various 
      congenital or acquired conditions. In this short series of three patients, one 
      had volvulus which was due to ligamentous laxity and mobile spleen, second had 
      congenital postero-lateral diaphragmatic defect and the third had hiatus hernia.
