TI  - Recurrent acute pancreatitis: an additional manifestation of the "wandering 
      spleen" syndrome".
PG  - 1034-8
AB  - A case of "wandering spleen" associated with recurrent pancreatitis and diagnosed 
      with computed tomography (CT), is reported. The entity was also associated with a 
      rotated, distended stomach, gastric outlet obstruction secondary to extrinsic 
      compression of the duodenum, and partial small bowel obstruction secondary to 
      extrinsic compression of a mobile, distended cecum that lay under the right 
      diaphragm.
