TI  - The wandering spleen.
PG  - 247-8
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare condition that commonly presents with splenic 
      infarction secondary to torsion. Splenectomy was previously advocated as the 
      treatment of choice, though recent reports suggest that the organ may be 
      distorted, and splenopexy performed. This paper documents how the latter 
      procedure may be done using adherent omentum.
