VI  - 40
IP  - 12
DP  - 1995 Dec
TI  - Wandering spleen with torsion in a geriatric patient. Report of an unusual case 
      with a brief review of the clinical picture and management.
PG  - 2656-9
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare condition that is extremely uncommon in the elderly. A 
      case of wandering spleen with torsion in a 73-year-old female is described in 
      detail. Our patient's presentation is unusual because in 1972, during a total 
      hysterectomy, she had no evidence of a wandering spleen. Preoperative 
      technetium-99 radionuclide liver-spleen studies were utilized to minimize the 
      potential for vascular difficulties. Splenectomy was the treatment of choice for 
      this condition and was performed to avoid splenic infarction. A review of the 
      literature and etiologic considerations are discussed.
