IS  - 0363-8715 (Linking)
VI  - 19
IP  - 1
DP  - 1995 Jan-Feb
TI  - Torsion of the wandering spleen: CT and angiographic appearance.
PG  - 84-6
AB  - OBJECTIVE: To seek CT and angiographic appearances that characterize torsion of 
      the wandering spleen. MATERIALS AND METHODS: The CT and angiographic findings of 
      two cases of preoperatively diagnosed torsion of the wandering spleen were 
      reviewed, and the findings were closely compared with intraoperative and 
      histopathological findings. RESULTS: Characteristic CT appearance seemed to be a 
      whirled appearance formed at the medial side of the displaced spleen. The 
      angiographic finding that was characteristic of the disease was a tapered and 
      abruptly twisted distal splenic artery. CONCLUSION: These findings were useful in 
      making the early and correct diagnosis of this rare but fulminant condition.
