PMID- 7950828
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19941221
LR  - 20190920
IS  - 0942-8925 (Print)
IS  - 0942-8925 (Linking)
VI  - 19
IP  - 5
DP  - 1994 Sep-Oct
TI  - Wandering spleen with torsion: appearance on CT and ultrasound.
PG  - 459-60
AB  - Wandering spleen is a rare entity which may present with symptoms suggestive of 
      other, more common abdominal processes. Torsion of the long pedicle may occur 
      causing abdominal pain. This article describes a case of wandering spleen 
      diagnosed by computed tomography (CT). Liver spleen scintigraphy and sonography 
      supported this diagnosis and suggested torsion. To our knowledge this is only the 
      second case of this entity in which color flow and duplex Doppler findings have 
      been reported.
