LR  - 20190830
IS  - 0301-0449 (Print)
IS  - 0301-0449 (Linking)
VI  - 24
IP  - 2
DP  - 1994
TI  - Torsion of the spleen: an unusual presentation of congenital diaphragmatic 
      hernia.
PG  - 150-1
AB  - We describe an unusual case of congenital diaphragmatic hernia in a 6-week-old 
      boy who presented with severe respiratory distress due to torsion of the spleen 
      which had passed up into the chest through a Bochdalek hernia and caused a left 
      hemothorax. Scintigraphy with heat-damaged red cells was diagnostic by showing a 
      damaged but functioning spleen above the diaphragm. Surgical repair and return of 
      the spleen to the abdomen resulted in complete recovery.
