DP  - 1994
TI  - Wandering spleen and gastric volvulus.
PG  - 535-6
AB  - Gastric volvulus and wandering spleen are related to anomalies in the 
      intraperitoneal visceral attachments. When encountered during infancy, they have 
      a congenital origin with acquired predisposing factors. Wandering spleen is a 
      rare clinical entity with a diverse form of presentation. To our knowledge, 
      gastric volvulus associated with wandering spleen has not been reported 
      previously in literature.
