DP  - 1994
TI  - Late-onset Bochdalek hernia with a rare postoperative complication: case report.
PG  - 306-7
AB  - We report a case of a 7-year-old-girl with a late-presenting Bochdalek hernia. 
      The postoperative course was complicated by splenic torsion and subsequent total 
      splenic infarction. Total splenic infarction due to splenic torsion has been 
      reported in children with "wandering spleen" and in incarcerated Bochdalek 
      hernias, but to our knowledge, not as a postoperative complication of Bochdalek 
      hernia repair.
