TI  - Torsion of wandering spleen: the whorled appearance of the splenic pedicle on CT.
PG  - 476-7
AB  - Congenital deficiency or acquired laxity of the suspensory ligaments of the 
      spleen may result in extreme splenic mobility. This rare condition, which is 
      termed wandering or ectopic spleen predisposes the elongated splenic pedicle to 
      torsion. We present a case of splenic torsion with a new CT finding consisting of 
      a whorled appearance of the splenic pedicle. To our knowledge this finding has 
      not been described before.
