PMID- 1595386
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19920702
LR  - 20071115
IS  - 0870-399X (Print)
IS  - 0870-399X (Linking)
VI  - 5
IP  - 3
DP  - 1992 Mar
TI  - [Torsion of wandering spleen. An unusual case of abdominal pain].
PG  - 152-4
AB  - Wandering spleen is uncommon and of difficult diagnosis. New Imaging Modalities 
      (Eco; TC), can suggest or confirm the preoperative diagnosis of wandering spleen, 
      permitting conservative surgery, mainly in children. We report two cases of 
      wandering spleen. The first one, with acute surgical abdomen and tumor on left 
      iliac fossa, operated as an ovarian cyst torsion: the laparotomy showed a 
      necrotic spleen in pelvis. The second case presented as intestinal sub-occlusion 
      with recurrent abdominal pain, and a left iliac fossa movable tumor. It was 
      diagnosed by eco and radionuclides before laparotomy. Even diagnosed in different 
      ways, the surgical treatment was the same.
