TI  - [Pedicle torsion of the accessory spleen within the scope of the 
      "polysplenia-asplenia complex" as a rare differential diagnosis of acute 
      abdomen].
PG  - 619-22
AB  - A 25 year old female patient with a painful palpable tumour in the right flank 
      was admitted to our hospital presenting signs and symptoms of an acute abdomen. 
      During explorative laparotomy unexpected haemorrhagic infarction of a splenula 
      caused by a volvulus of the vascular pedicle was found. In spite of the 
      documentation of multiple positional abnormalities of visceral organs 
      preoperative diagnostic imaging techniques were unable to point to the diagnosis 
      because of an uncommon rightsideness of the polysplenism. In the case of an 
      indefinite rightsided abdominal mass defects of embryonic morphogenesis should be 
      always taken into consideration.
