TI  - Torsion of an accessory spleen in an elderly patient.
PG  - 838-9
AB  - Torsion of an accessory spleen is recognized as a rare cause of acute abdominal 
      pain in childhood. A case is reported which, however, is unusual in that it 
      occurred in a patient of 75, who had had no previous symptoms which might have 
      suggested the presence of an accessory spleen.
