VI  - 117
IP  - 12
DP  - 1989 Dec
TI  - [Ectopic or migrating spleen and supernumerary spleens: detection and 
      identification with 99mTc, 51Cr and 113In radioisotopes].
PG  - 1403-8
AB  - Congenital malformations of the spleen are rare. We report a patient with an 
      ectopic spleen located in the left iliac fossa, which was excised in order to 
      prevent severe complications such as torsion of the pedicle, rupture or 
      infection. A second patient with idiopathic thrombocytopenic purpura presented 
      with an accessory spleen located retroperitoneally. Removal of this spleen 
      following removal of the normotopic one resulted in cure of purpura. The 
      clinical, radiological and radioisotopic studies used to locate and identify 
      these malformations are described.
