TI  - [Accessory spleen torsion. Clinical picture, sonographic diagnosis and 
      differential diagnosis].
PG  - 419-21
AB  - The torsion and infarction of an accessory spleen must be considered as a rare 
      cause of acute abdominal pain in childhood. It can be accompanied by acute 
      diffuse or localised abdominal pain and it could also appear to be an acute 
      appendicitis or an intussusception. The ultrasound examination helps to narrow 
      down the possible differential diagnoses.
