TI  - Splenic torsion and rupture in pregnancy.
PG  - 123-31
AB  - Splenic rupture in pregnancy and the puerperium is a rare and potentially 
      catastrophic event. A case of splenic rupture in pregnancy due to partial torsion 
      and internal trauma of a floating spleen is presented, and represents the 89th 
      pregnancy-puerperal report of splenic rupture. Nineteen additional cases have 
      been identified by the authors over the past 20 years. A 20-year review 
      (1967-1986) of clinical presentations, pathogenesis, and therapy are presented.
