PMID- 3622569
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19871022
LR  - 20190824
IS  - 0340-6997 (Print)
IS  - 0340-6997 (Linking)
VI  - 13
IP  - 4
DP  - 1987
TI  - Unusual case of an ectopic spleen.
PG  - 210-1
AB  - A rare case of a very unusual position of a normally functioning spleen in the 
      posterior aspect of the right lobe of the liver is reported. A 6-year-old boy was 
      evaluated with echocardiography for congenital heart disease of coexisting atrial 
      and ventricular septal defects with pulmonary hypertension. Other associated 
      cardiac abnormalities on this child included a right-sided aortic arch, drainage 
      of the azygous vein into the superior vena cava and an Eisenmenger complex. At 
      the time of echocardiography, absence of the spleen in its normal location was 
      noted. This prompted further investigation into localizing the spleen using 
      99mTc-sulfur colloid and heat denatured 99mTc-RBC scintigraphy. Both scans 
      demonstrated the spleen to lie posterior to the right hepatic lobe.
