PMID- 3746608
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19861010
LR  - 20190710
IS  - 0022-3468 (Print)
IS  - 0022-3468 (Linking)
VI  - 21
IP  - 8
DP  - 1986 Aug
TI  - Late return of function after intrathoracic torsion of the spleen in congenital 
      diaphragmatic hernia.
PG  - 722-4
AB  - A case of late presentation of a left posterolateral diaphragmatic hernia in a 
      four-year-old boy is reported. Shortly after incidental diagnosis of the 
      diaphragmatic hernia, he was admitted with acute abdominal symptoms and 
      laparotomy was performed. The stomach, small intestine, part of the colon, and 
      the spleen were intrathoracic. There was a 720 degree torsion of the splenic 
      pedicle. After reduction, the spleen was placed in the abdomen. At scintiscans 12 
      days and 14 weeks after operation, no certain splenic function was demonstrated, 
      but at follow-up up 21/2 years later the splenic scan was normal.
