VI  - 36
IP  - 2
DP  - 1985 Jun
TI  - Unusual position of the spleen--a report of two patients.
PG  - 163-5
AB  - An unusual position of the spleen may cause diagnostic difficulties and may mimic 
      disease. We report two patients with an unusual position of the spleen. In one, 
      congenital absence of the lieno-renal ligament allowed unusual mobility of a 
      bilobed spleen with intermittent torsion. In the other the spleen descended into 
      the left renal fossa following left adrenalectomy and nephrectomy.
