TI  - Torsion of a wandering spleen.
PG  - 181-2
AB  - We present an unusual case of torsion of a wandering spleen in a 14 year old boy. 
      Wandering spleen is an entity which has rarely been reported in infants and 
      children. Although patients may be asymptomatic, some may present as an acute 
      surgical emergency if trauma or torsion of the vascular pedicle occurs, as in our 
      case. The treatment of this condition is splenectomy.
