PMID- 3880638
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19850122
LR  - 20190717
IS  - 0196-0644 (Print)
IS  - 0196-0644 (Linking)
VI  - 14
IP  - 1
DP  - 1985 Jan
TI  - Splenic torsion presenting as a twisted hemorrhagic ovarian cyst.
PG  - 64-6
AB  - Torsion of a wandering spleen is rare, usually presenting as an acute abdomen and 
      commonly misdiagnosed. In our case, a 14-year-old girl was diagnosed 
      preoperatively as having a twisted hemorrhagic ovarian cyst. On laparotomy, an 
      infarcted spleen that was twisted on its pedicle was found in the lower abdomen. 
      The patient recovered uneventfully. The clinical spectrum of wandering spleen is 
      discussed briefly.
