VI  - 54
IP  - 6
DP  - 1984 Dec
TI  - Torsion of the spleen in the polysplenia syndrome.
PG  - 571-3
AB  - A case of splenic torsion is presented in an adult with the polysplenia syndrome. 
      The factors predisposing to splenic torsion are discussed. Splenic torsion may 
      mimic acute appendicitis. The recommended treatment is splenectomy. The 
      polysplenia syndrome may often be undiagnosed when cardiac defects are mild or 
      absent.
