PMID- 6468219
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19840928
LR  - 20190721
IS  - 0163-2116 (Print)
IS  - 0163-2116 (Linking)
VI  - 29
IP  - 9
DP  - 1984 Sep
TI  - Splenic torsion. An unusual cause of splenomegaly.
PG  - 868-71
AB  - A 28-year-old woman who presented with acute abdominal pain and splenomegaly was 
      found to have little functioning splenic tissue on liver-spleen scan but a large 
      homogeneous spleen by computerized axial tomography. Laparotomy revealed torsion 
      of the splenic pedicle and extensive splenic infarction. The presentation, 
      pathophysiology, and diagnostic difficulties of this case are discussed. Splenic 
      torsion should be considered in the differential diagnosis of painful 
      splenomegaly.
