TI  - [Wandering spleen with acute torsion of the pedicle].
PG  - 141-2
AB  - The A. A. describe one case of wandering spleen with torsion of the pedicle. In 
      spite of the rarity of this phenomenon and the vagueness of its clinical 
      manifestation, if this diagnosis is under consideration, it can be established by 
      angiography, by scintigraphy, or by sonography. After splenectomy the patient was 
      cured.
