PMID- 7120005
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19821202
LR  - 20220408
IS  - 0022-3468 (Print)
IS  - 0022-3468 (Linking)
VI  - 17
IP  - 4
DP  - 1982 Aug
TI  - Torsion of the wandering spleen: splenectomy or splenopexy.
PG  - 373-5
AB  - Torsion of the wandering spleen is a rare condition usually unsuspected 
      preoperatively. In previously reported cases in the past, attempts at splenopexy 
      have failed and splenectomy has been regarded as the treatment of choice. We are 
      presenting two children with splenic torsion. In one complete infarction of the 
      spleen had occurred and so splenectomy could not be avoided. In the second, the 
      spleen was viable and splenopexy was successfully performed. The clinical 
      presentation, etiology, diagnostic procedures and management are discussed, and a 
      surgical technique for splenopexy is described.
