TI  - Torsion of the spleen in a five-and-a-half-month-old infant.
PG  - 35-7
AB  - In this report, we describe torsion of the spleen in a five-and-a-half-month-old 
      infant, thus far the youngest reported patient in the literature. Celiac 
      angiography and tuftsin determination confirmed the clinical impression that the 
      pathology was confined to the spleen. The infant underwent a splenectomy and made 
      an uneventful recovery.
