TI  - Torsion of the wandering spleen seen as a migratory abdominal mass.
PG  - 36
AB  - Torsion of the wandering spleen is an unusual cause of an acute abdomen, rarely 
      diagnosed preoperatively. The authors describe a case which was suspected prior 
      to surgery and confirmed by radionuclide imaging. Radiographic findings include 
      an extrinsic mass on barium-enema examination and absence of the splenic shadow 
      in the left upper quadrant.
