PMID- 937848
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19760823
LR  - 20071115
IS  - 0003-1348 (Print)
IS  - 0003-1348 (Linking)
VI  - 42
IP  - 6
DP  - 1976 Jun
TI  - Chronic torsion of the spleen.
PG  - 427-9
AB  - Wandering spleen may result from congenital failure of splenic attachments or 
      acquired laxity of attachments due to stretching. The wandering spleen is quite 
      vulnerable to the complication of torsion, which is seen most often as an acute 
      abdominal emergency due to splenic infarction. A more unusual variant is chronic 
      torsion which causes intermittent mild to moderate abdominal pain, 
      gastrointestinal disturbances and, in one case, hypersplenism. A mass has been 
      present in most cases and may be anywhere in the abdomen or pelvis. Splenectomy 
      should be performed for all cases of wandering spleen with or without torsion.
