TI  - Torsion of a visceroptosed spleen.
PG  - 88-91
AB  - Torsion of the pedicle of a visceroptosed spleen, a rare condition, was diagnosed 
      preoperatively in a 4-year-old girl, with the aid of history, physical 
      examination, blood smear findings, splenic scans with technetium Tc 99m sulfur 
      colloid, and selective angiography. A splenectomy was performed, and the child 
      made an uneventful recovery. This case report illustrates some of the diagnostic 
      and therapeutic considerations pertaining to torsion of the spleen.
